 "input": "Hi team,\nWriting down how the branch runs because we keep getting it wrong. Reservations come from the central booking system; the branch pulls tomorrow's list every afternoon. Fleet controller assigns a car from the fleet list (by group and mileage). Prep team valets and fuels it and does the damage check on the check-out sheet with photos. At the counter, agent checks licence (DVLA check code) and takes the deposit hold on the card. On return, damage check again against the check-out sheet, any new damage goes to the damage claims team who bill the customer's deposit. Mileage and fuel recorded back into the fleet list. Cars due service are flagged by mileage in the fleet list and booked into the dealer.\nCheers, Ines",
